    "primary_concern": "Cell phones emit radio frequency (RF) energy, which could theoretically cause a spark that ignites fuel vapors. However, the energy levels involved in cell phone transmissions are extremely low. The RF energy emitted by a cell phone is not sufficient to generate a spark capable of igniting fuel vapors.",
