  "ACA_role": "In the United States, the Affordable Care Act (ACA), also known as Obamacare, has played a crucial role in addressing the issue of pre-existing conditions. Prior to the ACA, insurance companies could deny coverage or charge significantly higher premiums based on an individual's health status. The ACA mandated that insurance companies could not deny coverage or charge more based on pre-existing conditions, which was a significant step towards ensuring that all individuals, regardless of their health status, could access health insurance.",
  "ongoing_challenges": {
