text:
{
  "headline": "The headline highlights the increasing diagnosis of sleep apnea, a serious condition characterized by pauses in breathing during sleep. These pauses can last from a few seconds to minutes and can occur multiple times throughout the night, leading to poor sleep quality and various health issues such as high blood pressure, heart disease, and diabetes. The good news is that sleep apnea can be effectively managed with a device called a Continuous Positive Airway Pressure (CPAP) machine. This machine delivers a steady stream of air pressure through a mask worn during sleep, keeping the airways open and allowing for uninterrupted breathing. The use of a CPAP machine can significantly improve the quality of sleep and overall health for those suffering from sleep apnea, offering a simple yet effective solution to this common and potentially dangerous condition."
}

